# S'more Skills camp sync

This is a **community** addon. Guild is only a small marker (“a guildie is at this fire”), not how camps travel.

Design: **Forever first.** [CAMPING.md](../../CAMPING.md). TBC Anniversary is only the two-client testbed while Forever servers are down — do not ship Anniversary-shaped UX (profession-icon sockets, Classic-only APIs). Forever uses the **retail/Mainline addon API and restrictions** (not Classic) — see [FOREVER.md](../../FOREVER.md).

## Never

- Use GUILD / PARTY / RAID as the share channel
- Ask the guild (or anyone) to dump camps on login
- Auto-broadcast stored camps when someone joins
- Reuse another addon's message prefix
- Apply a camp from the other faction
- Let more than three object slots exist on a camp
- Scan the whole continent for fires — addons only see what is in range or what others share
- Block the UI thread on addon messages — cap pins, drop stale signals

## Required

- Hidden custom channel `SmoreSkills`. Prefix `SmoreSk`
- Payload under 250 bytes per message. If `H:` is over, shrink (drop want-items, then object names, then shorten `own`) — do not fail silent
- Message types:
  - `S:` seeker — `S:map:fac:prof:t[:codes]:layer` (looking in zone; last field is zoneUID or `0`)
  - `H:` host — `H:map:x:y:fac:own:want:p1:o1:p2:o2:p3:o3:t:layer` (`layer` is `zoneUID` or `zoneUID/N`; optional; we detect it ourselves)
  - `X:` packed up — `X:map:x:y:own:t` (host right-clicks own pin; seekers drop it now)
  - `C:` legacy camp snapshot — still accepted if received; we no longer send it
- Share is **opt-in**: seek / host only when the player acts
- Same-faction only
- Three slots. Each player places at most one object (the game enforces that; we display it)
- Cooldowns: seek 45 s, host rebroadcast 90 s, outbound 8 s per player (`X:` skips the 8 s cooldown)
- Signal TTL ~3 min; campfire pin ~20 min from when the fire was lit (same remaining time for every seeker; heartbeats do not extend it) or until full/packed/replaced; forget camps older than 30 minutes
- Max 12 pins per zone
- Host pin is **local**; other host pins only after **Find** (and an `H:`). Do not show C: snapshots as pins
- Answering a seek does **not** `SendChatMessage` or `SendAddonMessage` from `CHAT_MSG_*` or a timer (taints). Channel-chat `H:` is sent on the next Find or `/smores host` click. Addon whisper only if the channel is not joined, and only from that click.
- One player, one hosted camp. A **new** campfire packs the previous pin (`X:`) and hosts the new site. Walking away or `/smores host` without a new fire keeps the original fire coords. `/reload` restores the hosted camp from SavedVariables until pack / 3/3 / pin TTL.
- World map pins are **hosts only** — seekers do not get a pin; do not show C: snapshots as pins
- Do not call `ChatFrame_RemoveChannel` (taints chat). Auto-host must not `SendChatMessage`, `SendAddonMessage`, or `JoinPermanentChannel` from UNIT_SPELLCAST / CHAT_MSG_* / OnUpdate / WorldFrame / C_Timer. After the fire lands, host locally; send hidden-channel **chat** `H:` on the next Find or `/smores host` click. Do not hook WorldFrame / UIParent or EnableKeyboard. Other host pins only after Find. Continent **overview** (EK / Kalimdor) has no pins; a continent-typed **leaf** map (Zephras Isle) still draws.
- Do not occupy `/1` General, `/2` Trade, or `/3` Local Defense. Join the named channel with `JoinChannelByName` (no chat window). Send by name/id after join. If we land on 1–3, swap **by channel index** (`C_ChatInfo.SwapChatChannelsByChannelIndex`) with the zone channel that belongs there (`General - Zephras Isle` still counts as General). Snap the edit box off `[n. SmoreSkills]`.
- Keep broadcasting the **fire coords** if the host walks away (do not key hosting to current feet)
- Nested city maps (Elwynn/Stormwind, Dun Morogh/IF, Durotar/Org): still draw **zone** pins if `GetMapID()` is the city. Sibling zones (Elwynn vs Duskwood) must not share 39,70-style pins. Forever new zones (Zephras Isle, Hyjal, Shen'dralas, Riverglades) use the same C_Map rules — do not hardcode an Elwynn-only list.
- Guild mark is optional UI, not a requirement to see or share a camp
- TBC Anniversary (`20505`/`20506`) for two-client testing while Forever servers are down. Forever `## Interface:` when beta FrameXML is known. Forever is Mainline API (secrets, chat lockdown), not Classic. Sockets show the **camping object** (live item texture, then stored stand-in); profession icon only if the slot names a trade and no object.
